  { q: 'What are the most common SQL syntax errors?', a: 'The most frequent are unbalanced parentheses and unclosed string quotes, both of which the Best Answer Hub SQL Formatter detects. Missing commas between columns, a missing table after FROM or JOIN, and a stray semicolon are also common. Structural issues are caught here; missing-table errors need a real database to surface.' },
